  "Number": 11,
  "Question": "The angle formed by the hands of a clock at \\(2:15\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(30^\\circ\\)",
    "B": "\\(27\\frac12^\\circ\\)",
    "C": "\\(157\\frac12^\\circ\\)",
    "D": "\\(172\\frac12^\\circ\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The hour hand moves continuously between hour marks. The \\(12\\) equal gaps around the clock each measure \\(360^\\circ/12=30^\\circ\\).\n\nAt \\(2{:}15\\), the minute hand points at \\(3\\). In the \\(15\\) minutes since \\(2{:}00\\), the hour hand has traveled one quarter of the gap from \\(2\\) to \\(3\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{15}{60}\\cdot30^\\circ\n=7\\frac12^\\circ.\n\\]\nThe remaining angle between the hour hand and the minute hand is therefore\n\\[\n30^\\circ-7\\frac12^\\circ\n=22\\frac12^\\circ.\n\\]\nThis smaller angle is absent from choices A through D, so the answer is \\(\\mathrm{E}\\), none of these.",
